# 33. FORKLIFT STATUS

Main states:

WAITING
    ↓
CLAIMED
    ↓
IN_PROGRESS
    ↓
COMPLETED

Possible:

WAITING → CANCELLED

CLAIMED → CANCELLED

IN_PROGRESS → FAILED

Invalid status transitions must be rejected.

---

# 34. FORKLIFT CLAIM CONCURRENCY

This is a critical business requirement.

Two operators must NEVER be able to claim the same ForkliftJob.

Example:

Operator A clicks CLAIM.

Operator B clicks CLAIM at the same time.

Only one operator succeeds.

The backend and database must guarantee this.

Do NOT rely on frontend locking.

The operation must be atomic.

Conceptually:

UPDATE ForkliftJobs
SET
    Status = CLAIMED,
    OperatorId = CurrentOperator,
    ForkliftId = CurrentForklift,
    ClaimedAt = CurrentTime
WHERE
    Id = JobId
    AND Status = WAITING

If no row is updated:

Return conflict.

Message:

"Container đã được nhân viên khác nhận."

---

# 35. FORKLIFT LOCATION

Always distinguish:

FromLocation
PlannedLocation
ActualLocation

Example:

From:

GATE / INSPECTION AREA

Planned:

A-03-02-01

Actual:

A-03-02-02

Do not automatically assume:

Actual = Planned.

When the operator confirms completion, the system must capture ActualLocation.

